"'''Lightsaber Lost'''" is the eleventh episode of [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|Season Two]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series. It aired on [[January 22]], [[2010]] after the series went on a two week hiatus.

==Official description==
''When a wily pickpocket steals Ahsoka's lightsaber, she enlists the help of an ancient Jedi to track down her weapon and reclaim her honor.''

==Opening narration==
{{OpeningCrawl
|name=Episode 11<br />LIGHTSABER LOST
|text=War creates opportunity for the criminal
underworld! Ruthless mercenaries
conspire with the Separatists to disrupt
and exploit the unstable situation within
the Republic.

Now, Anakin Skywalker and Ahsoka
Tano descend into the treacherous
gangster havens in an effort to find a
corrupt and vile arms dealer who is
buying weapons on the black market and
selling them to the Republic's enemies....}}

==Plot summary==
{{Quote|A thief stole my lightsaber, and I only got a quick look at him.|Ahsoka Tano, to Tera Sinube|<ref name="Lost" />}}
[[Anakin Skywalker|Anakin]] and [[Ahsoka Tano|Ahsoka]] are in the slums of [[Coruscant]] searching for [[Car Affa]], an arms dealer selling Republic weapons to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]]. They arrive at a bar where Affa is hiding, and Anakin instructs Ahsoka to wait outside while he apprehends the fugitive. When the patrons storm out of the bar, Ahsoka is jostled to the ground by the crowd. When she realizes her [[lightsaber]] is missing, she catches a glimpse of it in the hands of a pickpocket. She chases the thief, but loses him in the crowd. Unwilling to inform Anakin about her loss, she heads to the [[Jedi Archives|Archives]] in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] in hopes that Jocasta Nu can help her find the thief. She proves no help at all due to her limited knowledge of Coruscant’s criminal element, but hope is not lost because she is able to serendipitously direct her towards the one person who can help: [[Tera Sinube]], a [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] with specialized knowledge about Coruscant's criminal underworld. Sinube finds Ahsoka's thief in the database, a [[Patrolian]] named [[Bannamu]]. Before Ahsoka rushes off, Sinube insists that he comes along on her adventure, advising her that slowing down will help her find what she's looking for.

Back in the slum district, they are directed to Bannamu's hideout—the [[Spider Arms Hostel]]. Ahsoka eventually locates Bannamu, and learns that he has sold her [[lightsaber]] to an assassin called [[Nack Movers]]. The two Jedi hurry to find him, while Sinube advises Ahsoka again to be patient in their search. At the apartment owned by Movers' girlfriend, they find that the lock has been cut open and Movers has been killed. The two Jedi soon see a frightened female called [[Ione Marcy]] hiding in the apartment, who asks if the men who killed Movers have gone. Ahsoka goes to search the bedroom, where she gets attacked by [[Cassilyda Cryar|Cassie Cryar]], wielding Ahsoka's lightsaber. Upon learning that Ahsoka is a Jedi (not knowing she’s a Padawan training as a Jedi, that is), Cassie jumps through the window and runs away along the city's rooftops. Ahsoka chases after her and contacts Sinube, informing him about the development.

Sinube realizes an inconsistency due to the fact that Ahsoka's attacker was a female while Ione Marcy claims that [[Gender|men]] had broken into the apartment. Coupled with sensing something more than just shock in her, Sinube deduces that Ione Marcy was involved in the crime. He subtly attaches a [[Homing beacon|tracking device]] to her and summons [[GU-series Guardian police droid]]s, but Ione escapes in an [[airspeeder]].

Meanwhile, Ahsoka is closing on Cassie on the top of a high building, when Cassie jumps and lands in Ione's passing speeder. Sinube picks up Ahsoka in another speeder, and they follow the tracking device to a [[train]] station. Police droids apprehend Ione, but Cassie manages to dash off onto the top of a departing train. Ahsoka runs after her and they ultimately enter a wagon, where Cassie takes a [[Twi'lek]] mother and child as hostages, still with Ahsoka's lightsaber in her hand. When the train arrives at the next station, Cassie attempts to run away again, but Sinube, having gotten to the station first, intercepts her and disarms her. Cassie is arrested. Later, Sinube suggests that Ahsoka should share the lesson she has learned as they head to the Jedi Temple. Master Yoda greets them and invites Ahsoka to share with the [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] the value of patience and the responsibilities of never losing their lightsabers.

==Continuity==
The flashback in this episode contains a scene from the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|Season One]] finale, "[[Hostage Crisis]]." Although aired first, according to [https://www.starwars.com/news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder the official chronology] those events would not occur until well after those of "Lightsaber Lost."

After realizing her lightsaber is missing, Ahsoka exclaims: "My master is gonna kill me!". This is a nod to Anakin saying a nearly identical line upon realizing [[Anakin Skywalker's first lightsaber|his lightsaber]] was destroyed in the [[Geonosis droid factories|Geonosis droid factory]] in [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']]. Additionally, Ahsoka tells the Younglings: "This weapon is your life.", a line spoken by [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] to Anakin when the former returns the latter's lightsaber while searching for [[Zam Wesell]] on [[Coruscant]]. 

At the end of the episode, Master Sinube tells Ahsoka to "pass on what you have learned", a line spoken by Yoda to [[Luke Skywalker]] just before the former's death in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']]. 

When Ahsoka visits Jocasta Nu in the Jedi Archives Library, a criminal file on [[Brea Tonnika]] is open on the computer Nu is using. The Aurebesh text next to her picture reads "LAST SEEN ON CORUSCANT WANTED FOR MURDER."

When Ahsoka is looking for a lightsaber to buy near the noodle bar, behind her on the wall is written "[[Unidentified massage parlor|Massage]]."

When Ahsoka and Master Sinube are walking down the hall toward Nack Movers' apartment, Ahsoka's sash keeps clipping through the bottom of her skirt.

When Ahsoka is chasing Cassie Cryar, numerous floating advertising boards they jump over feature [[Aurebesh]] writing. One such board reads "SODA," another reads "[[Star Tours|STAR TOURS]] GLEE ANSELM CALL 1-800-555-6576 NOW!" The text under [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] reads "[[Kuat Drive Yards|KUAT DRIVE YARDS]] AWARD" before being cut off.

Despite the fact that one of the floating ads Ahsoka jumps on involves Palpatine making a speech and that the speech is included in the quotes on the episode guide, neither the character nor [[Ian Abercrombie]], the [[Supreme Chancellor]]'s usual voice actor, appear in the credits.

A list of destinations that pops up at the [[hovertrain]] station has [[Burbank]] listed, a reference and in-joke to [[Wikipedia:Burbank, California|the town]] in [[California]]. A similar in-joke would appear later in the Season 5 episode, "[[To Catch a Jedi]]."

[[Pablo Hidalgo]] mentioned that Cassie Cryar and Ione Marcy were intended to have been lovers.<ref>{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/703684857121996800|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-02-27|quote=For those talking about the subject, note that Cassie Cryar and Ione Marcy were written as a couple in a relationship.|archivefile=File:CassieCryar_IoneMarcy_PabloHidalgo_tweet.png|nolive=1}}</ref>

The episode is based on the classic 1949 [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akira_Kurosawa Akira Kurosawa] film ''[[Wikipedia:Stray Dog (film)|Stray Dog]],'' which revolves around a newly promoted Japanese police detective attempting to recover his stolen pistol with the aid of a veteran investigator.

The ending of the episode has two stained glass [[Unidentified veranda (Jedi Temple)|windows]] that aren't completely visible that depicted [[Valenthyne Farfalla]] leading the [[Army of Light/Legends|Army of Light]], and Farfalla and [[Jedi Lord|Lord]] [[Hoth (Jedi Lord)|Hoth]] from the comic book series ''[[Star Wars: Jedi vs. Sith]]''.<ref name="Jedi vs. Sith">''[[Star Wars: Jedi vs. Sith]]''</ref><ref name="TCW CS2">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Two|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season Two]]</ref>

